==English==
===Meaning===
To earn enough to survive.

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb|head=[[keep]] the [[wolf]] from the [[door]]}}

# {{label|en|idiomatic}} To [[ward off]] [[poverty]] or [[hunger]].
#: ''They didn't earn much, but it was enough to '''keep the wolf from the door'''.''
# {{label|en|idiomatic}} To delay sexual [[ejaculation]].

===Origin===
A very old saying used from at least from 1647.<ref>Vol 3 of familiar letters, James Howell, publisher Humphrey Moseley, St Pauls Churchyard, 1655, page 8, copy of letter from 1647</ref>

===Translations===
{{trans-top|to ward off poverty}}
